{#
  commitizen's stock CHANGELOG.md.j2 (4.19.0), plus one include.

  A release can carry hand-written notes in .github/release-notes/<tag>.md, for
  example .github/release-notes/v3.8.0.md. When that file exists it is rendered
  directly under the version heading, ahead of the sections commitizen builds
  from commits. It exists for releases whose version number understates them:
  v3.8.0 carries breaking changes in a minor bump, and users pinned to <4 get no
  semver signal, so the changes have to be stated where they read the changelog.

  The notes file is loaded as a Jinja template, so it must not contain Jinja
  delimiters. tests/unit/test_release_line_workflow.py renders this template.
#}
{% for entry in tree %}

## {{ entry.version }}{% if entry.date %} ({{ entry.date }}){% endif %}


{% include ".github/release-notes/" ~ entry.version ~ ".md" ignore missing %}

{% for change_key, changes in entry.changes.items() %}

{% if change_key %}
### {{ change_key }}
{% endif %}

{% for change in changes %}
{% if change.scope %}
- **{{ change.scope }}**: {{ change.message }}
{% elif change.message %}
- {{ change.message }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
